# Copy to `.dev.vars` for local `wrangler dev`. RUNTIME secrets only.
#
# .env is BUILD time (Astro reads it through import.meta.env, and every public
# page is prerendered). .dev.vars is REQUEST time: it is what the Worker's
# `cloudflare:workers` env holds, and it is the only way the SSR routes added on
# 2026-09-06 can read a token.
#
# WHICH ROUTES CARE
#   /preview/**            draft-aware pages for the Studio Presentation tool
#   /preview/live          the SSE proxy that streams edits into the preview
#   /api/draft-mode/enable the draft-mode handshake
#
# All of them fail CLOSED without a token: they answer 503 naming what is
# missing rather than a stack trace. With a token, an unauthenticated GET of
# /api/draft-mode/enable answers 401 "Invalid preview secret", which is the
# quickest way to tell the two states apart.
#
# NOTE for `wrangler dev -c dist/server/wrangler.json`: wrangler looks for
# .dev.vars next to the CONFIG, so copy this file to dist/server/.dev.vars for
# that command (dist/ is gitignored, so it is a scratch copy).
#
# In production and on staging these are Worker SECRETS, not vars:
#   npx wrangler secret put SANITY_TOKEN --name 2ndpreschicago
#   npx wrangler secret put SANITY_TOKEN --name 2ndpreschicago-staging
# A build-time variable in Workers Builds is NOT enough: it never reaches the
# request-time env.

# A Sanity READ token (Viewer permission). Nothing in the preview path writes.
# SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN is accepted as an alias, since this repo already ships
# a build-time read token under that name.
SANITY_TOKEN=
